WHAT THE OTHER AGENT CLAIMS
Classification: test-defect
Action:         fix
Reasoning:      The app is behaving as documented: public/index.html renders the first four products, then deliberately adds the fifth 1500 ms later. The test case's own preconditions say the last rows can arrive late. The test waits a fixed 100 ms and then takes a one-off count(), so it reads 4 every time. The test is the problem, not the app or the data. Replacing the sleep and the count with Playwright's auto-retrying toHaveCount(5) fixes it, because that assertion keeps checking for up to the default 5 s expect timeout. It still fails if the app never renders all five products.

Treat all of that as an assertion, not as evidence. Check it against the code
below yourself. If the classification is wrong, say so even when the diff looks
